.TH setools-mcp 1 2026-08-19 "SELinux Project" "SETools: SELinux Policy Analysis Tools"

.SH NAME
setools-mcp \- SELinux policy analysis server for Model Context Protocol clients

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setools-mcp
.RB [ \-\-policy PATH ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.RI [ CONFIG ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B setools-mcp
runs a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server exposing SETools SELinux policy analysis tools.
The server communicates over the stdio transport when no configuration file is supplied.
When a configuration file is supplied, it communicates over HTTP and uses the file's bind
address, port, and authentication settings.

Authentication applies only to the HTTP transport. The stdio transport relies on the security
of the local execution environment.

.SH CONFIGURATION
.I CONFIG
is an optional path to an INI-format configuration file parsed by
.BR setools.mcp.config.MCPConfig .
The file may contain a
.B [server]
section with
.B host
and
.B port
options, an
.B [auth]
section selecting an authentication method, and one section containing options for that method.

The supported authentication methods are
.BR none ,
.BR jwt ,
.BR static ,
.BR debug ,
.BR introspection ,
.BR remote ,
.BR oauth_proxy ,
and
.BR oidc_proxy .
The full OAuth authorization-server implementation,
.BR OAuthProvider ,
is not supported by the configuration file.

The
.B remote
and
.B oauth_proxy
methods require a nested token verifier selected with the
.B token_verifier
option. The verifier is configured in its corresponding section, such as
.BR [jwt] .

See
.I docs/MCP-CONFIG.md
and the example files in
.I docs/
for the complete option reference and provider-specific examples.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "--policy PATH"
Use PATH as the default SELinux policy file for analysis.
.TP
.IP CONFIG
Load CONFIG as the MCP server configuration file. Supplying CONFIG selects the HTTP transport;
omitting it selects stdio.
.TP
.BR \-v , \-\-verbose
Print additional informational messages.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debugging output and display Python warnings by default.
.TP
.BR \-h , \-\-help
Display help information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
Start the server over stdio without authentication:
# setools-mcp

Start an HTTP server using the JWT configuration example:
# setools-mcp docs/mcp-auth-jwt.ini

Start an HTTP server on the configured address with verbose logging:
# setools-mcp -v /etc/setools/mcp.ini
.fi

.SH FILES
.TP
.I docs/MCP-CONFIG.md
Configuration format and authentication option reference.
.TP
.I docs/mcp-auth-*.ini
Example configuration files for each supported authentication method.

